 "simulation": {
  "notes": "Simulated counterparties (plans/counterparty.py). No external system is contacted: each program / vendor slot is an in-process adapter whose dispositions are drawn deterministically from a seeded scenario (seed = workspace | patient | program | plan as_of, one independent uniform draw per stage and attempt), so the same plan always gives the same outcomes. Rates are per program below (synthetic planning assumptions for engineering tests, not measured performance of any vendor). Modifiers multiply a stage probability when a patient fact holds; results are clipped to [0.01, 0.97].",
  "timestamp_hours": [
   9,
   17
  ],
  "followups": {
   "unreachable": {
    "type": "pcp_notice",
    "owner": "attributed_practice",
    "due_days": 14,
    "detail": "patient not reached after outreach attempts; ask the attributed practice to raise the program at the next visit"
   },
   "declined": {
    "type": "pcp_notice",
    "owner": "attributed_practice",
    "due_days": 14,
    "detail": "patient declined; clinician-authorized revisit"
   },
   "eligibility_denied": {
